WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.799 --> 00:00:04.630
If we find aliens, what do we do next?

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:09.420
When discussing first contact, many are quick
to point out that historically, contact between

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:15.440
culturally different civilizations has almost
always led to the destruction of one of those

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:16.440
civilizations.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:21.720
Because of this, you could argue that we should
stick to ourselves, leave the aliens alone,

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:27.149
but in almost every one of those historical
examples its the civilization that makes contact

00:00:27.149 --> 00:00:30.979
that destroys the civilization that receives
contact.

00:00:30.979 --> 00:00:35.760
So perhaps we should go on the offensive—find
the aliens before they find us.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.390
Of course, we’ve been trying for decades
to find extraterrestrial life.

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:43.179
It’s one of humanity’s great questions—are
we alone?

00:00:43.179 --> 00:00:48.219
One way we might find aliens is by looking
at stars—or more specifically, the light

00:00:48.219 --> 00:00:49.410
level of stars.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:52.749
As the earth has developed, our energy consumption
has skyrocketed.

00:00:52.749 --> 00:00:57.010
That’s just the consequence of an increasingly
technologically advanced world.

00:00:57.010 --> 00:01:01.600
It’s suspected that this trend will continue
and it’s also suspected that with any alien

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:06.190
civilization, they’ll also require more
and more energy as they advance.

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:10.520
Eventually, any planetary civilization will
reach a point where the amount of energy on

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:14.580
their planet is not enough to sustain their
advancing civilization.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:19.400
Theoretical Physicist Freeman Dyson speculated
that when a planetary civilization needs more

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:23.540
energy than their planet can provide, they’ll
turn to the sun.

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:28.210
Stars are the most abundant source of energy
in any planetary system so a super-advanced

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:33.640
civilization can build a series of satellites
to orbit around their sun to collect energy.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:38.290
When sunlight travels through space, it looses
energy and so the amount of energy captured

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:44.000
by a solar panel near the sun would be astronomical
higher than a solar panel on earth.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.971
With more energy a civilization could produce
more satellites and eventually there would

00:01:47.971 --> 00:01:50.490
be a swarm of satellites orbiting the sun.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:55.750
Freeman Dyson believes that this is the most
logical way that any civilization would harvest

00:01:55.750 --> 00:02:00.290
the energy they need so if we search for a
star with orbiting satellites, we might be

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:03.140
able to find an alien civilization.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:08.009
No telescope is powerful enough to see the
individual satellites, but we can rather easily

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:10.390
observe the light levels of stars.

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:14.790
You see, once a faraway civilization builds
enough satellites, the swarm will start to

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:18.420
block our view of their sun as the satellites
orbit.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:23.470
From our perspective, it will look like the
star is twinkling—something completely unnatural.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:28.680
So, by looking for stars with highly variable
light levels, we might be able to find an

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:32.530
alien civilization harvesting the energy of
their sun.

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:39.200
KIC 8462852, also known as Tabby’s star,
is a star in the Cygnus constellation of the

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.260
Milky Way.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:44.840
Scientists observed the light level of this
star for years, and they regularly came across

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:46.970
irregularities like this.

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:51.350
Maybe there are comets or a debris field obstructing
our view of the star, but astronomers have

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:55.180
doubted that either of these could dip the
light levels by this much.

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:59.709
This has led some to suggest that an alien
civilization has built these orbiting satellites

00:02:59.709 --> 00:03:02.670
around their sun…but we may never know for
certain.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:07.500
Of course all of this is somewhat speculative
and its unlikely that we’d actually find

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.190
a so-called Dyson sphere around a sun.

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:14.080
It’s more of a thought-experiment—demonstrating
that we could find aliens through looking

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:16.230
for their impact on the universe.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:20.410
Conversely, aliens might find us based on
our affect on the universe.

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:26.400
That’s why we’ve very purposefully sent
out messages to our hypothetical cosmic neighbors.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:30.870
The Pioneer Plaques were designed and placed
on the two Pioneer spacecrafts which were

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:34.490
the first to explore the far-reaches of the
solar system.

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:38.710
Since these two are some of the farthest man-made
objects from earth, they were sent with a

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:42.610
message in case extraterrestrials come across
the probes.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:45.450
This is what was sent—the Pioneer Plaque.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:50.060
It has a representation of hydrogen—the
most abundant element in the universe—;

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:54.520
a picture of a man and women including a raised
hand—a gesture that most likely wouldn’t

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:59.660
be understood but shows how our limbs move
and the existence of the opposable thumb;

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:03.920
an image of the pioneer spacecraft behind
the humans so that extraterrestrials could

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:09.810
figure out the rough size of humans; the location
of the sun relative to 14 nearby pulsar stars

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:14.590
using hydrogen spin-flip transition frequency
as the unit—something far too complicated

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:19.220
for me to explain; and lastly an image of
the solar system with the rough trajectory

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:23.840
of the pioneer spacecraft; but there are issues
with this image.

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:28.219
We have no idea how aliens gather information.

00:04:28.219 --> 00:04:32.449
Humans are a visual species since we have
relatively good vision so its natural for

00:04:32.449 --> 00:04:34.979
us to convey information through images.

00:04:34.979 --> 00:04:39.969
Aliens, on the other hand, could have poor
or no vision and therefore no conception of

00:04:39.969 --> 00:04:45.199
the idea of transferring information through
images or they could interpret the symbols

00:04:45.199 --> 00:04:46.710
vastly differently.

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:50.520
Perhaps the most frequently criticized aspect
of the plaque is the arrow.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:54.770
Its believed that the arrow symbol is derived
from either the shape of arrows or the human

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:58.139
hand pointing, or perhaps a combination of
both.

00:04:58.139 --> 00:05:03.169
Aliens would most likely have neither arrows
or hands and therefore no idea what this symbol

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:04.169
means.

00:05:04.169 --> 00:05:08.589
They could also make the dangerous assumption
that the symbol depicts a weapon launching

00:05:08.589 --> 00:05:11.710
meaning that the spacecraft was sent to harm
them.

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:16.599
Other sets of images have been sent with subsequent
space probes, but the chance of aliens finding

00:05:16.599 --> 00:05:20.569
these few tiny objects in the vastness of
space is miniscule.

00:05:20.569 --> 00:05:25.039
What’s far more likely is that aliens will
discover humanity off of something we’ve

00:05:25.039 --> 00:05:28.969
been sending out for over a hundred years—radio
signals.

00:05:28.969 --> 00:05:33.159
While most are too weak to reach far-away
galaxies, some do travel through space and

00:05:33.159 --> 00:05:39.009
could be picked up by extraterrestrial civilizations—especially
more advanced ones with better detection technology

00:05:39.009 --> 00:05:40.009
than us.

00:05:40.009 --> 00:05:43.759
It’s entirely possible that we’ve already
unintentionally sent the signal that will

00:05:43.759 --> 00:05:46.759
be our first message to an extraterrestrial
civilization.

00:05:46.759 --> 00:05:51.650
It’s also entirely possible that the first
sign we will have of extraterrestrial life

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:53.830
is a radio message from another planet.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.729
The problem is then deciphering it.

00:05:55.729 --> 00:05:58.719
The first step is deciding what the message
even is.

00:05:58.719 --> 00:06:02.620
Is it binary, is it radiation, is it natural
language, what is it?

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:04.150
We can figure this out.

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:09.460
In the English language, the most common word,
“the,” accounts for about 7% of all word

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:15.509
occurrences, the second most common word,
“be”, accounts for 3.5% of all words,

00:06:15.509 --> 00:06:19.550
then “and” is about 2.3% and so on and
so forth.

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:24.979
The distribution of words, it turns out, in
all languages follows a logarithmic scale.

00:06:24.979 --> 00:06:29.699
The second most common word occurs about half
a frequently as the most common, the third

00:06:29.699 --> 00:06:36.060
1/3 as often, the fourth 1/4th as often, the
fifth 1/5th as often and so on and so forth.

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:41.439
This is somehow true for all languages—even
ones with no common ancestral language—which

00:06:41.439 --> 00:06:46.099
means that, more than likely, an alien language
will follow the same distribution.

00:06:46.099 --> 00:06:51.029
It’s not entirely understood why languages
follow this distribution, but one possible

00:06:51.029 --> 00:06:53.669
explanation is that people are lazy.

00:06:53.669 --> 00:06:55.849
It’s called “the Principle of Least Effort.”

00:06:55.849 --> 00:07:01.210
People, animals, even machines will always
pick the path of least resistance—the easiest

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:05.379
path—and in the case of language, the meaning
that needs to be most frequently conveyed

00:07:05.379 --> 00:07:10.460
will be attached to the most common word rather
than a number of other words since that is

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:11.460
easiest.

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:15.879
That keeps happening down to the least frequent
word therefore creating this distribution.

00:07:15.879 --> 00:07:20.719
With an extraterrestrial transmission, if
we rank the sounds by frequency and it follows

00:07:20.719 --> 00:07:25.289
this distribution, we can believe that its
most likely a language.

00:07:25.289 --> 00:07:28.219
But then we need to try to understand the
language.

00:07:28.219 --> 00:07:31.349
For this, we need to drop all assumptions.

00:07:31.349 --> 00:07:36.099
There are innate similarities across all human
languages, mostly related to grammar.

00:07:36.099 --> 00:07:42.969
For example, pretty much every language separates
description words—nouns—from action words—verbs.

00:07:42.969 --> 00:07:48.710
Grammatically, there are huge similarities
between all languages—even ones that developed

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:49.710
separately.

00:07:49.710 --> 00:07:54.809
Some have suggested that this means that humans
have a genetic framework for language.

00:07:54.809 --> 00:08:00.059
Perhaps we are hardwired from birth to understand
what nouns and verbs and sentences are and

00:08:00.059 --> 00:08:05.159
learning a language is just the process of
filling in and understanding that framework.

00:08:05.159 --> 00:08:10.210
From everything we understand about the communication
systems that animals use, they do not have

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:12.379
a universal grammar like humans.

00:08:12.379 --> 00:08:16.939
We therefore have to assume that an alien
language will be fundamentally different than

00:08:16.939 --> 00:08:17.939
ours.

00:08:17.939 --> 00:08:20.149
We don’t know how they’ll structure sentences.

00:08:20.149 --> 00:08:22.460
We don’t even know if they’ll have sentences.

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:27.249
The problem is, if we just receive a natural
language transmission, there’s really nothing

00:08:27.249 --> 00:08:28.399
we can do.

00:08:28.399 --> 00:08:33.459
When deciphering ancient languages, linguists
figure out meaning using context and relations

00:08:33.459 --> 00:08:38.839
to other languages, but with an alien language
transmission there is no context and no other

00:08:38.839 --> 00:08:41.269
similar languages to compare it with.

00:08:41.269 --> 00:08:46.170
All this is assuming that aliens use a verbal
language, and that’s a huge assumption.

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:50.320
Many if not most animals have no verbal communication
system.

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:54.649
Cuttlefish and Chameleons alter their body
color to communicate while ants and honeybees

00:08:54.649 --> 00:08:57.930
use pheromones to talk to other members of
their species.

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:01.680
Even if we understood their language, could
we understand what they’re saying?

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:03.410
Take this sentence in French.

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:07.870
Translating it literally word for word you
get “The palace Bourbon is the name commonly

00:09:07.870 --> 00:09:12.180
given to the building that houses the assembly
national french located on the quay of Orsay

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:15.440
in the seventh borough of Paris of the square
of the Concorde.”

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:19.779
Even if you clean it up to structure it like
an English sentence, how much meaning is conveyed

00:09:19.779 --> 00:09:20.779
to you?

00:09:20.779 --> 00:09:25.470
What exactly is the French National Assembly,
where is the Quay of Orsay, where is the seventh

00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:28.350
borough, where is Concorde Square?

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:32.089
Someone familiar to Paris and France would
understand what these words mean but someone

00:09:32.089 --> 00:09:35.750
from the other side of the world would infer
little meaning from them.

00:09:35.750 --> 00:09:40.500
Philosopher Ludwig Wittgenstein famously wrote,
“If a lion could speak, we would not be

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:42.529
able to understand him.”

00:09:42.529 --> 00:09:47.130
Language is all based on cultures and requires
a common frame of reference.

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:50.500
If you said “I’m taking an Uber to get
some coffee at Starbucks” to an English

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:53.120
speaking Lion, there’s no way it would understand
what you’re saying.

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:57.639
You’d have to explain what Uber is, then
explain what a car is, what the internet is,

00:09:57.639 --> 00:10:02.500
what a phone is, an app, coffee, Starbucks,
stores, the monetary system—all stuff that

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:04.800
is intuitive to modern humans.

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:09.519
Translating the words of an extraterrestrial
civilization is just the first step, understanding

00:10:09.519 --> 00:10:12.390
what they’re saying is the more difficult
task.

00:10:12.390 --> 00:10:17.040
Centuries or millennia after detecting aliens,
we might reach a day when an extraterrestrial

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:18.730
being comes to earth.

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:23.600
If this happens, the alien civilization is
almost certainly more advanced than humans

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:28.620
since it has accomplished interstellar travel
and perhaps even faster-than-light travel,

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:31.820
but we want to show that us humans are intelligent
as well.

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:32.820
Of course the E.T.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:36.579
would see everything the humans have built,
but they might interpret the structures of

00:10:36.579 --> 00:10:39.240
man-kind as natural phenomenons.

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:43.120
We can’t assume that they’d think that
buildings and cars and artificial light are

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:45.819
not part of the natural structure of earth.

00:10:45.819 --> 00:10:50.420
We therefore need to show them that we have
at least a basic understanding of the universe.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:53.160
Math, as far as we know, is universal.

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:58.220
No matter where you go or who you ask, two
plus two is four and the ratio of a circle’s

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:03.589
circumference to diameter is 3.141592 and
so on and so forth.

00:11:03.589 --> 00:11:07.910
Of course what you call two or four or pi
would be different, but the concepts are the

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:08.910
same.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:15.050
Therefore, we could show the aliens our understanding
of math—put two then two then four; four

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:18.639
then four then eight; keep this going until
they get the point.

00:11:18.639 --> 00:11:23.480
Although, perhaps the best mathematical principle
to demonstrate would be the pythagorean theorem.

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:25.899
It’s complicated, but easy to show.

00:11:25.899 --> 00:11:30.379
The Pythagorean Theorem, of course, demonstrates
that in the case of a right triangle, the

00:11:30.379 --> 00:11:35.050
square of the side opposite to the right angle
is equal to the square of the other two sides

00:11:35.050 --> 00:11:36.050
combined.

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:39.690
In an equation that reads a2 + b2 = c2.

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:44.509
Visually, we can demonstrate this by drawing
squares on the two shorter sides out of smaller

00:11:44.509 --> 00:11:48.959
squares and show how the amount of squares
on the two sides equals the amount of squares

00:11:48.959 --> 00:11:50.430
on the longer side.

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:55.370
Showing this theorem cements that humans do
understand how the mathematical aspect of

00:11:55.370 --> 00:11:59.329
the universe works, even though we’re less
advanced than the aliens.

00:11:59.329 --> 00:12:04.350
So now that we’ve found the aliens, now
that we’ve met them, we can talk to them,

00:12:04.350 --> 00:12:05.800
someone needs to speak first.

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:10.399
But let’s say it was you—let’s say you
were given the chance to ask the first question

00:12:10.399 --> 00:12:15.120
from humanity to an extraterrestrial being,
you became the first point of contact between

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:18.079
humanity and the universe.

00:12:18.079 --> 00:12:19.670
What would you ask?

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:23.220
